|> Exercise
    work=ing
    handle=_verbal_to_arithmetic_A_change_

    If $A$ is a function of time, meaning
    that we can write
    “$A(0.2)$”
    to denote “the value of $A$ at time $t = 0.2$”, etc,
    then how to write

    __the change in $A$ between $t = 11.199$ and
    $t = 11.2$__

    mathematically?
    !! (No trick.)

    |> Solution

        This is

        |> Boxed
            $$
            A(11.2) - A(11.199)
            $$

        or, literally, “the value of $A$ at $t = 11.2$ minus the value
        of $A$ at $t = 11.199$”.
